  "interpretation": [
    "The observed standardized conditional coefficient remains unusual under all three predeclared topology-null count-error simulations.",
    "Sharing current-year census error between N_eff and the growth denominator does not generate an observed-scale positive coefficient under the fixed Poisson or 10%/20% Gamma-Poisson sensitivities.",
    "Median paired coupling bias is -2.3%, +0.8%, and +8.8% of the observed beta under Poisson, CV10%, and CV20% respectively.",
    "This supports retention of N_eff only as a conditional same-census association, not as a robust held-out-year predictive result.",
    "The simulations are stylized sensitivities, not empirically calibrated Palmer observer-error models."
  ],
  "manuscript_consequence": "Withdraw the positive predictive claim and report the permutation p=0.262. If N_eff remains in the manuscript, describe beta +0.1168 as a conditional association that survives the fixed mechanical-coupling sensitivities, while explicitly noting that its out-of-year error reduction is not stronger than the year-block permutation null.",
  "next_gate": "Reframe the manuscript and journal target; do not open further topology metrics or error-model tuning for the core paper."
}
